  "notes": {
    "confidence": "verbatim",
    "printed": [
      "1. LONG-TERM IS STATIONARY WORK THAT OCCUPIES A LOCATION MORE THAN 3 CONSECUTIVE DAYS",
      "2. TEMPORARY / INTERIM PAVEMENT MARKINGS SHALL BE USED AS SHOWN, OR IN ACCORDANCE TO THE CONTRACT DOCUMENTS. ANY EXISTING PAVEMENT MARKINGS THAT ARE CONFLICTING OR MISLEADING SHALL BE REMOVED OR COVERED",
      "3. THE TEMPORARY POSITIVE BARRIER SHALL NOT BE PLACED ALONG THE MERGING TAPER. THE LANE SHALL BE CLOSED USING CHANNELIZING DEVICES AND PAVEMENT MARKINGS",
      "4. TYPE B HIGH INTENSITY FLASHING WARNING LIGHTS ARE REQUIRED ON THE SIGNAL AHEAD SIGNS (W3-3). FLASHING WARNING LIGHTS ARE RECOMMENDED ON THE ROAD WORK AHEAD SIGNS (W20-1) AND ONE LANE AHEAD SIGNS (W20-4) AND MAY BE USED TO INCREASE TARGET VALUE AND VISIBILITY, AS DETERMINED BY THE ENGINEER",
      "5. REFER TO MUTCD FOR ADDITIONAL TRAFFIC SIGNAL REQUIREMENTS",
      "6. DETECTORS SHALL BE INSTALLED ON ALL APPROACH LANES AND ALL PHASES SHALL BE ACTUATED. DURATION OF RED CLEARANCE INTERVALS SHALL BE ADEQUATE TO CLEAR THE ONE-LANE SECTION OF CONFLICTING TRAFFIC. OM3-R (TYPE",
      "7. THE TRAFFIC SIGNAL CYCLE SHALL REST IN RED. WHEN THE SIGNAL IS CHANGED TO MARKER THE FLASHING MODE, EITHER MANUALLY OR AUTOMATICALLY, RED SIGNAL INDICATIONS SHALL BE FLASHED TO ALL APPROACHES",
      "8. STOP LINES SHALL BE INSTALLED WITH TEMPORARY TRAFFIC SIGNALS FOR INTERMEDIATE AND LONG-TERM CLOSURES. EXISTING, CONFLICTING PAVEMENT MARKINGS AND RAISED PAVEMENT MARKINGS, BETWEEN THE ACTIVITY AREA AND THE STOP LINE, SHALL BE REMOVED. AFTER THE TEMPORARY TRAFFIC SIGNAL IS REMOVED, THE STOP LINES ROAD AND ALL TEMPORARY PAVEMENT MARKINGS SHALL BE REMOVED AND PERMANENT PAVEMENT MARKINGS RESTORED. WORK XX",
      "9. WHERE NO-PASSING LINES ARE NOT ALREADY IN PLACE, THEY SHALL BE ADDED FOR A DISTANCE OF 500'-600' FROM THE STOP BAR. ANY EXISTING PAVEMENT MARKINGS THAT ARE CONFLICTING OR MISLEADING SHALL BE REMOVED OR COVERED",
      "10. ADJUSTMENTS IN THE LOCATION OF ADVANCED WARNING SIGNS SHOULD BE MADE TO ACCOMMODATE THE HORIZONTAL AND VERTICAL ALIGNMENT OF THE ROADWAY, RECOGNIZING THAT THE DISTANCES SHOWN FOR SIGN SPACING ARE MINIMUMS. ADJUSTMENTS IN THE HEIGHT OF THE SIGNAL HEADS SHALL BE MADE AS NEEDED TO CONFORM TO THE VERTICAL ONE ONE LANE LANE ROAD ROAD ALIGNMENT. AHEAD YY",
      "11. THE SUPPORTS FOR TEMPORARY TRAFFIC CONTROL SIGNALS SHALL NOT ENCROACH INTO THE MINIMUM REQUIRED WIDTH OF A \"PEDESTRIAN ACCESS ROUTE\" OF 4'",
      "12. THE ENGINEER MAY REQUIRE THE USE OF AN ADVISORY SPEED PLAQUE (W13-1) TO TYPE SUPPLEMENT A WARNING SIGN. THE PLAQUE WILL BE USED TO INDICATE AN ADVISORY FLASHING SPEED FOR THE WORK ZONE CONDITION. (IE. NARROW LANES, BUMPS, POOR ROADWAY SURFACE, LOW OR NO SHOULDER, DROP-OFFS, GEOMETRIC CONSTRAINTS, AND/OR POOR SIGHT CONDITIONS)",
      "13. WHEN LOOP DETECTORS ARE USED, A POINT LOOP SHOULD BE PLACED 50' FROM THE STOP BAR, AND CALLING LOOP SHOULD BE PLACED AT OR NEAR THE STOP BAR FOR WHEN A SIDE ROAD OR DRIVEWAY IS BETWEEN THE STOP BAR AND POINT LOOP. ON NIGHTTIME WORK",
      "N1. WORK OCCURRING AFTER SUNSET AND BEFORE SUNRISE WILL BE CONSIDERED STOP STOP NIGHTTIME OPERATIONS. HERE HERE ON ON RED RED",
      "N2. ALL SIGNS, STOP/SLOW PADDLES AND RED FLAGS USED TO WARN/ALERT/CONTROL TRAFFIC SHALL BE RETROREFLECTIVE",
